---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { RELEASES, SUBMIT_LOG, REPO } from "../lib/data";
import { SITE } from "../config";
const commands = [
  ["/fscout", "Status: sessions, events, route points, items missing from Questie"],
  ["/fscout pause", "Stop recording (resume with /fscout resume)"],
  ["/fscout share on", "Allow automatic uploads by the uploader app (off to stop)"],
  ["/fscout note <text>", "Drop a note at your spot, like \"cave is packed\" or \"skip, elite\""],
  ["/fscout gear", "Copy your equipped gear into the BIS planner on this site"],
  ["/fscout report", "Copyable list of quests and NPCs Questie is missing"],
  ["/fscout export", "Copyable export string of your recorded sessions"],
  ["/fscout wipe confirm", "Erase everything recorded"],
];
---
<Base image="/og/scout.jpg" title="ForeverScout" description="ForeverScout is a free WoW Forever addon that records how long quests really take and where Forever's new items drop, so other players can find new gear.">
  <h1>ForeverScout</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A small, read-only addon that records how you level and what you loot: quests, XP, where
    things are, how long each one took, and which items drop from where. Your logs replace our
    estimates with real numbers.
  </p>
  <div class="itemrec">
    <h2>It records items too</h2>
    <p>Forever adds gear Classic never had, and most of it has no known source yet. Every time you loot something green or better, ForeverScout notes the item and the NPC or chest that dropped it. <b>Each recording helps other players find new gear and new items.</b> Once two different players have seen a drop, its item page shows "Confirmed in Forever by N players" next to that source, in the <a href="/items/">item database</a> and the <a href="/bis/">BIS planner</a>. Sources that only Classic-era data lists stay marked as unconfirmed until someone loots them.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>How your logs show up</h2>
  <div class="showup">
    <section>
      <h3>A badge on the item page</h3>
      <p>When two different players loot the same item from the same mob or chest, that source gets a <span class="confirmed">Confirmed in Forever by 2 players</span> badge on the item page, in its tooltip and in the BIS planner. The count goes up as more players see it.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Your name on the leaderboard</h3>
      <p>Every quest you time and every drop you log earns points on the <a href="/leaderboard/">Scout leaderboard</a>, with 3 extra for each drop you find first that someone else then confirms. The Discord's <b>#leaderboard</b> channel shows the standings and a weekly Scout report (<a href={SITE.discord} rel="noopener">join the Discord</a>). Your name there is an anonymous one like <b>Scout 97800d</b>, shown by the uploader when you set it up.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="dl">
    {SITE.curseforge && <a class="btn" href={SITE.curseforge} rel="noopener">Get it on CurseForge</a>}
    <a class={SITE.curseforge ? "btn secondary" : "btn"} href={RELEASES}>Download from GitHub</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href={SITE.discord} rel="noopener">Get help on Discord</a>
  </p>
  <p class="small muted">Free and open source. Works with or without Questie. Available on CurseForge and GitHub.</p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Add the addon</h3>
      <p>Download <code>ForeverScout-x.y.z.zip</code> and unzip the <code>ForeverScout</code> folder into your Forever client's <code>Interface\AddOns\</code> folder.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Log in and choose sharing</h3>
      <p>You'll see "ForeverScout: recording your route." Pick <b>Share automatically</b> if you want your log sent for you.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Install the uploader (optional)</h3>
      <p>From the same release, run <code>ForeverScoutUploader.exe</code> (Mac builds are there too) and choose <b>Yes</b>. It sends your log after each logout or <code>/reload</code>.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Play normally</h3>
      <p>That's all. Type <code>/fscout</code> any time to see what's been recorded.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>No uploader? Zip <code>WTF\Account\&lt;ACCOUNT&gt;\SavedVariables\ForeverScout.lua</code> from your Forever folder and attach it to a <a href={SUBMIT_LOG}>Submit a log</a> issue.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What it records</h2>
  <div class="two">
    <div>
      <h3>Recorded</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Quests accepted, turned in and abandoned, with the NPC and your position</li>
        <li>XP gained and where it came from: quest, kill (mob and level) or other</li>
        <li>Objective progress, like "Mottled Boar slain: 3/10", and which quest it belongs to</li>
        <li>Dungeon and raid boss fights: the boss, group size, whether it was a kill, and how long it took</li>
        <li>Items you loot (green or better, or any gear) and which NPC or chest dropped them, so the BIS planner knows where Forever's new items come from</li>
        <li>Your position about every 10 seconds while moving, plus flights, deaths and hearthstones</li>
        <li>Class, race, faction, level and game build</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Never recorded</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Character name, realm, account name or GUID. Each character gets a random ID that never leaves your computer.</li>
        <li>Chat, whispers or other players</li>
        <li>Gold, bag contents or anything outside questing and loot</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">ForeverScout only reads what the game shows you. It never plays, clicks or automates anything.</p>

  <h2>How your data is used</h2>
  <p>Shared logs are combined every few hours. Only totals across players reach the site; individual logs are never published.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What the addon records</th><th>Where it shows up</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Quest accept and turn-in times, quest XP</td><td>Measured minutes and XP per minute on <a href="/quests/">quest pages</a>, replacing estimates; the <a href="/guides/">leveling guides</a> will use them to pick faster routes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Objective progress and where it happened</td><td>The <b>Objective areas</b> map on each quest page. A spot only appears once two or more players progressed there.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Loot and its source</td><td>Drop sources for Forever's new items in the <a href="/items/">item database</a> and <a href="/bis/">BIS planner</a>, with a "Confirmed in Forever" badge once two players have seen the drop</td></tr>
        <tr><td>How many quests and drops your logs add</td><td>Your points on the <a href="/leaderboard/">Scout leaderboard</a>, under an anonymous scout name</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Boss fights in dungeons and raids: which boss, group size, kill or wipe, and how long it took</td><td>Kill counts, wipes and typical kill times on the <a href="/raids/">dungeon and raid pages</a>. A boss only shows once two or more players logged it, and one pull counts once however many group members recorded it. Who was in the group is never recorded.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>New quests and NPCs</td><td>Missing quests, givers and XP on this site, and fixes sent to Questie</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Route points, flights, deaths, hearthstones</td><td>Coming next: real travel times between quest hubs for route scoring, and a warning on quests where players die a lot</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What's new</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Objective tracking:</b> objective progress now notes which quest it belongs to, so quest pages can show where players actually finish each objective. Nothing new about you is recorded.</li>
    <li><b>Objective areas on quest pages:</b> spawn points for every kill, object and drop objective, with a <code>/way</code> line you can paste into TomTom.</li>
    <li><b>Quest chains:</b> every quest in a chain now links back and forward correctly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>ForeverScout and best in slot</h2>
  <p><b>Today:</b> <code>/fscout gear</code> copies the gear you're wearing into the <a href="/bis/">BIS planner</a>, so it starts from your character and shows which slots to upgrade first. It's a copy and paste: your gear isn't uploaded. Loot logs fill in where each Forever item drops.</p>
  <p><b>What we're changing:</b> the planner's stat weights are set by hand per role today, so talents, race and hit caps don't change the result. Next, weights will come from simulations of each spec using <a href="https://github.com/wowsims/forever">wowsims/forever</a>, an open-source Forever simulator, and then take your talents, race and caps into account.</p>
  <p><b>After launch, if you choose to share:</b> ForeverScout will be able to record a snapshot of the gear you have equipped, so the planner can show what players of each spec actually wear. That would only appear once at least 10 accounts share for a spec, with one count per character per day. It will be listed on this page before it's turned on, and it stays off if sharing is off.</p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{commands.map(([c, d]) => <tr><td><code>{c}</code></td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Using Questie too?</h2>
  <p><code>/fscout report</code> lists quests and NPCs missing from Questie's Forever database, ready to paste into Questie's Discord. Confirmed findings also go upstream from this project. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>How fixes reach Questie</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .itemrec { margin: 0.4rem 0 1.4rem; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; max-width: 80ch; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--xp); border-radius: 10px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--xp) 8%, var(--surface)); }
  .itemrec h2 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .itemrec p { margin: 0; }
  .showup { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 0 2rem; }
  .showup h3 { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .confirmed { display: inline-block; padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; font: 600 0.72rem var(--font-body); color: var(--bg); background: var(--xp); white-space: nowrap; }
  .dl { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; counter-reset: s; max-width: 70ch; }
  .steps li { counter-increment: s; position: relative; padding-left: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(s); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.1rem;
    width: 2rem; height: 2rem; display: grid; place-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--xp-fill); color: #fff; border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .steps h3 { margin: 0 0 0.2rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .steps p { margin: 0; }
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 0 2rem; }
  .two h3 { font-size: var(--step-1); }
</style>
